# Operator cheat sheet. Static text only — no probes, no service calls.
cat <<'EOF'
============================================================
                 SHIELD XL LIGHT CONSOLE
============================================================

CONNECTIONS

SSH:
  ssh light@shieldxl-light.local

Known LIGHT-CONTROL address:
  192.168.88.246

QLC WEB:
  http://shieldxl-light.local:9999
  http://192.168.88.246:9999


------------------------------------------------------------
LIGHT CONSOLE
------------------------------------------------------------

STATUS:
  systemctl status light-console --no-pager

RESTART:
  sudo systemctl restart light-console

LOG:
  journalctl -u light-console -n 100 --no-pager


------------------------------------------------------------
QLC+
------------------------------------------------------------

STATUS:
  systemctl status qlcplus --no-pager

STOP:
  sudo systemctl stop qlcplus

START:
  sudo systemctl start qlcplus

RESTART:
  sudo systemctl restart qlcplus

LOG:
  journalctl -u qlcplus -n 100 --no-pager

WEB:
  http://shieldxl-light.local:9999

Runtime is qlcplus.service:

  /usr/bin/qlcplus-qml -w -o /home/light/shows/master.qxw

That is the production Pi pattern. -o is a flag; the path is positional.
WebAccess can take several minutes after a large workspace loads.
Do not SIGTERM during Refresh 2D view.
Do not use -9 or POST /loadProject.

SHOWS remain logical groups. Interactive show control is deferred.

If qlcplus.service is stopped:

  sudo bash /home/light/light-console/scripts/restore-qlc.sh

or:

  sudo systemctl start qlcplus


------------------------------------------------------------
APPLIANCE CHECK
------------------------------------------------------------

Read-only. Does not start, stop, or restart services.

  cd /home/light/light-console
  python3 -m light_console.appliance_check

or:

  /home/light/light-console/packaging/light-appliance-check


------------------------------------------------------------
SHOW PROJECTS
------------------------------------------------------------

Canonical master workspace (content), not loaded automatically:

  /home/light/shows/master.qxw

Logical show metadata:

  ls -l /home/light/shows/*.yaml

OLED:

  MENU -> SHOWS -> E1 select -> K3

K3 activates that logical show. It does not load QLC.


------------------------------------------------------------
IMPORT SHOW FROM MAC
------------------------------------------------------------

Run on the Mac, not inside Shield SSH:

  cd /Users/miiroseppanen/shieldxl-light-console

  ./scripts/import-show.sh --name "SHOW A" --dry-run "/path/to/show.qxw"

Dry-run prints SOURCE -> MASTER ID mapping and does not write master.qxw.


------------------------------------------------------------
MANUAL FILE COPY
------------------------------------------------------------

These scp commands are run from the Mac terminal.

FROM MAC TO SHIELD:

  scp "/path/to/file.qxw" \
    light@shieldxl-light.local:/home/light/

For show projects, prefer ./scripts/import-show.sh --dry-run instead of
copying directly into /home/light/shows/ or onto current.qxw.

FROM SHIELD TO MAC:

  scp light@shieldxl-light.local:/home/light/<file> .


------------------------------------------------------------
PROJECT / REPOSITORY
------------------------------------------------------------

Runtime/deploy path:
  /home/light/light-console

The deployed tree is an rsync copy, not a Git checkout.

  cd /home/light/light-console
  python3 -c "from light_console import VERSION; print(VERSION)"

Mac repository:
  /Users/miiroseppanen/shieldxl-light-console

  cd /Users/miiroseppanen/shieldxl-light-console
  git describe --tags --always
  git rev-parse --short HEAD


------------------------------------------------------------
POWER
------------------------------------------------------------

Preferred shutdown:
use the OLED:
  SYSTEM -> SHUTDOWN -> CONFIRM

Terminal fallback:

  sudo /usr/sbin/shutdown -h now

The sudoers rule intentionally allows only this shutdown
command passwordlessly, not general sudo.


------------------------------------------------------------
IMPORTANT
------------------------------------------------------------

- Production Pi is a separate machine:
  valot@192.168.88.248

- Do not copy production .qxw directly over active Shield files.
  Use the Shield upload/import workflow.

- Do not run multiple Shield light-console instances.
  systemd owns the runtime instance.

- Real lighting outputs are currently disabled/not configured
  during Milestone 0.6 unless later milestones explicitly change this.


------------------------------------------------------------
LAUNCHPAD
------------------------------------------------------------

Expected device:
  USB 1235:0036
  ALSA name: Launchpad Mini MIDI 1

STATUS:
  lsusb
  aconnect -l

QLC 5.2.2 does not hotplug-rescan MIDI devices.
Connect the Launchpad before QLC starts. qlcplus.service waits a
short bounded time for it, then starts anyway if it is missing.

If the Launchpad was attached after QLC was already running:

  sudo systemctl restart qlcplus

That restart needs the light user password (sudoers does not
allow passwordless systemctl). It does not restart light-console.

Do not match the pad by ALSA client number; that number changes.


------------------------------------------------------------
Show this help anytime:

  light-help

============================================================
EOF
